games.description:
UpEnglish helps you learn the English words and phrases you actually need: for work, travel, study, interviews, shopping, cafes, and everyday situations.

Start with ready-made popular topics or build your own dictionary. Add words and phrases, get translations and pronunciation, organize vocabulary into categories, and come back to it through focused practice.

What’s inside:

• ready-made collections on popular topics;
• a personal dictionary for your own words and phrases;
• AI collections: describe a situation, and the app will suggest useful vocabulary;
• 5 practice modes: flashcards, quiz, reverse translation, word building, and writing;
• pronunciation and audio for words;
• levels, XP, stats, and achievements to track your progress.

Preparing for a conversation with a landlord, your first day at work, a Python interview, a trip, or ordering breakfast at a cafe? Create a topic and practice the words you’ll actually use in real life.

Learn more than random word lists. Build your own living vocabulary, practice it in different ways, and turn new expressions into confident active knowledge. Learn English words for your real goals: ready-made topics, your own dictionary, AI collections, pronunciation, and 5 practice modes. Translate and Memorize

"Tap &amp; Talk: First Words" is a calm learning game for toddlers (ages 1–5).

Two modes:
Play - tap icons and learn new words with a friendly guide character.
Quiz - review and check what your child has learned.

Inside:
-topics: pets, vehicles, farm, colors, home objects;
-real photos and sounds;
-voiced word names + short, simple facts;
-Auto Play - plays automatically, no tapping needed;
-no timers, no rush - your child sets the pace.

For parents:
-no sign-up, no accounts;
-protected parental section (before purchases and settings);
-extra topics unlock with a one-time purchase (full access). A calm learning app for ages 1-5: real photos, sounds, voice, and Auto Play. Extra topics unlock with a one-time purchase. Parental section is protected. First words for toddlers
